# .NET Project and Build Rules

## Solution Structure
- Solution file (`.sln`) at the repository root
- Production projects in `src/`, test projects in `tests/`
- Use `Directory.Build.props` at the solution root with shared properties
- Use `Directory.Packages.props` with `<ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>true</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>`

## Required MSBuild Properties (in Directory.Build.props)
```xml
<PropertyGroup>
  <TargetFramework>net9.0</TargetFramework>
  <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
  <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
  <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
</PropertyGroup>
```

## NuGet Package Management
- When central package management is enabled, omit `Version` from `<PackageReference>` in project files
- Add new packages only after checking for known vulnerabilities
- Prefer `Microsoft.Extensions.*` abstractions for cross-cutting concerns

## Build Commands
```bash
dotnet restore         # Restore packages
dotnet build           # Build (debug)
dotnet build -c Release  # Build release
dotnet test            # Run tests
dotnet format          # Auto-fix formatting
```
